{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"d64fe227e7268b99","name":"card_unit_devils_brigade","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/WinterWar/units/card_unit_devils_brigade","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DEVIL'S BRIGADE","text":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to an enemy. If it is a unit with Alpine, destroy it instead.","flavorText":"The Devil’s Brigade, also known as The Black Devils or officially as the 1st Special Service Force, was an elite American–Canadian commando unit which was formed in 1942 and fought in WWII. The unit was known for its rigorous training in specialized skills like parachuting, skiing, rock climbing, amphibious operations, and other abilities that were crucial to their missions. The brigade saw combat in Italy and France between 1943 and 1944 and earned a reputation for audacious and effective missions behind enemy lines. Though unconfirmed, the unit was referred to as both the Black Devils and the Devil's Brigade by the Germans, with the latter being their preferred name. They were also known for having cards printed with their insignia and the message \"Das dicke Ende kommt noch!\" (\"The worst is yet to come\") written in red ink, which they left on deceased German soldiers to invoke psychological warfare. In December 1944, a combination of politics and a new military strategy caused the Devil's Brigade to be disbanded, but those who had survived filled in as replacements in Allied Airborne Divisions. However, despite its short lived service during WWII, the modern American and Canadian special operations forces trace their heritage to this unit.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.commando"],"Name":"card_unit_devils_brigade","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_devils_brigade_title","SourceString":"DEVIL'S BRIGADE","LocalizedString":"DEVIL'S BRIGADE"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_devils_brigade_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to an enemy. If it is a unit with Alpine, destroy it instead.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Deal 1 damage to an enemy. If it is a unit with Alpine, destroy it instead."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_devils_brigade_history","SourceString":"The Devil’s Brigade, also known as The Black Devils or officially as the 1st Special Service Force, was an elite American–Canadian commando unit which was formed in 1942 and fought in WWII. The unit was known for its rigorous training in specialized skills like parachuting, skiing, rock climbing, amphibious operations, and other abilities that were crucial to their missions. The brigade saw combat in Italy and France between 1943 and 1944 and earned a reputation for audacious and effective missions behind enemy lines. Though unconfirmed, the unit was referred to as both the Black Devils and the Devil's Brigade by the Germans, with the latter being their preferred name. They were also known for having cards printed with their insignia and the message \"Das dicke Ende kommt noch!\" (\"The worst is yet to come\") written in red ink, which they left on deceased German soldiers to invoke psychological warfare. In December 1944, a combination of politics and a new military strategy caused the Devil's Brigade to be disbanded, but those who had survived filled in as replacements in Allied Airborne Divisions. However, despite its short lived service during WWII, the modern American and Canadian special operations forces trace their heritage to this unit.","LocalizedString":"The Devil’s Brigade, also known as The Black Devils or officially as the 1st Special Service Force, was an elite American–Canadian commando unit which was formed in 1942 and fought in WWII. The unit was known for its rigorous training in specialized skills like parachuting, skiing, rock climbing, amphibious operations, and other abilities that were crucial to their missions. The brigade saw combat in Italy and France between 1943 and 1944 and earned a reputation for audacious and effective missions behind enemy lines. Though unconfirmed, the unit was referred to as both the Black Devils and the Devil's Brigade by the Germans, with the latter being their preferred name. They were also known for having cards printed with their insignia and the message \"Das dicke Ende kommt noch!\" (\"The worst is yet to come\") written in red ink, which they left on deceased German soldiers to invoke psychological warfare. In December 1944, a combination of politics and a new military strategy caused the Devil's Brigade to be disbanded, but those who had survived filled in as replacements in Allied Airborne Divisions. However, despite its short lived service during WWII, the modern American and Canadian special operations forces trace their heritage to this unit."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment","EHelpBubbleTypes::Blitz","EHelpBubbleTypes::Alpine","EHelpBubbleTypes::Exile"],"hasDeployment":true,"hasBlitz":true,"hasAlpine":true,"exileNation":"EFactionEnum::Britain","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_use_devils.t_use_devils","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Top","artist":"US WW2 poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DEVILS_BRIGADE.DEVILS_BRIGADE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":503.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_devils_brigade_photo","SourceString":"Men of the Devil’s Brigade being briefed before setting out on a patrol, Anzio beachhead, Italy, 1944.","LocalizedString":"Men of the Devil’s Brigade being briefed b